ith its administrative capital in Saigon (present-day Ho Chi Minh City). In the face of recurring peasant unrest, and of growing political agitation in Saigon, the French operated a plantation economy whose primary strategic product was rubber.\nAfter the end of the Japanese occupation (1941–1945) and the expulsion from Saigon of the Communist-led, nationalist Viet Minh in 1946, the territory was reorganized by the French as the Autonomous Republic of Cochinchina, a decision that helped trigger the First Indochina War. In a further move to deny the claims of the Democratic Republic of Vietnam declared in Hanoi by the Viet Minh, in June 1949 Cochinchina was united with the protectorates of Annam and Tonkin under their former de jure emperor Bảo Đại as the State of Vietnam within the French Union."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q19955896","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q105076326","value_label":"Saigon","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Saigon"},{"qid":"Q19955896","kind":"language","value_qid":"Q9199","value_label":"Vietnamese","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P2936","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Vietnamese"},{"qid":"Q19955896","kind":"successor","value_qid":"Q10748344","value_label":"Provisional Central Government of Vietnam","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P156","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Provisional Central Government of Vietnam"},{"qid":"Q19955896","kind":"flag","value_qid":null,"value_label":"Flag of France.svg","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P41","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":null},{"qid":"Q19955896","kind":"flag","value_qid":null,"value_label":"Flag of Republic of Cochinchina (variant).svg","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P41","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":null},{"qid":"Q19955896","kind":"coat","value_qid":null,"value_label":"Coat of arms of French Cochinchina - Album Artistique de la France & de ses Colonies (1900).svg","from_t":null,"to_t"